{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>A red one (אדמוני).</b> The yod is added; it is extraneous." "And the word כאדרת is not in construct state — rather its whole sense is: \"all of him was like a hairy garment (כאדרת)\" — and according to others, it is in construct state." "<b>And they called his name.</b> Those who saw him. And it is possible that the meaning is that it is a separate event, and this birth was a great wonder, because every human being emerges with an afterbirth that covers him, and behold, the two afterbirths opened at one moment."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:45:49.149445171Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}